{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvK5b6dbFDJh1HbAoJbW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Most likely cause: an Agent is a Durable Object built on PartyServer, and it needs to know its **name**. `getAgentByName()` and `routeAgentRequest()` pass that name in when they get the stub. `idFromString()` (like `newUniqueId()`) gives you a stub for a bare hex ID with no name attached, so the Agent never sets `this.name`. When your RPC method runs, anything that reads the name or depends on it (state, SQL setup, `onStart`, scheduling, broadcasting) throws, usually with an error like \"Attempting to read .name … before it was set.\"\n\nThe fix is to address Agents by name: `const stub = await getAgentByName(env.MyAgent, \"some-name\")`, then call `stub.myMethod()`. If you only have an ID string, keep a mapping back to the name you used and look it up that way. I answered from memory of the Agents SDK and didn't check your code, so if your error message is different, paste it and I'll take another look."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5811,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5811},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fac30c9d-09fe-4ebb-b28f-469a5b68ed85","uuid":"3b20a816-87cd-4960-a8c2-4d78b343550e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:44:08.849Z","request_id":"req_011CfvK5aqm7uQJE486g6E35"}
